  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Segundo condicional**",
      "",
      "| Estructura | Uso | Ejemplo |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| *If + pasado simple, would + verbo* | situación **imaginaria** o poco probable (presente / futuro) | *If I **won** the lottery, I **would travel**.* |",
      "",
      "**Comparación con el primer condicional**",
      "",
      "| Primero (real) | Segundo (imaginario) |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| *If I **win**, I'**ll** buy a car.* (es posible) | *If I **won**, I'**d** buy a car.* (casi imposible) |",
      "| *If it **rains**, we'**ll** stay.* | *If it **rained**, we'**d** stay.* (hipótesis) |",
      "",
      "**Reglas**",
      "",
      "- El pasado después de *if* **no es pasado real**: es hipótesis. Por eso en *to be* se usa *were* con todos: *If I **were** rich … · If she **were** here …* (en coloquial *was*, pero *were* es más correcto).",
      "- Contracciones: *would = 'd · would not = wouldn't.*",
      "- Preguntas: *What **would** you do if you **won** a million?* · *Would you quit if you were rich?*",
      "- También: *could* (podría) y *might* (quizá): *If I had time, I could learn Italian.*",
      "",
      "**Consejo con If I were you:** *If I were you, I'd tell the truth.* (= yo en tu lugar…)",
      "",
      "**Errores típicos**",
      "",
      "- ✘ *If I would win* → ✔ *If I won*. ✘ *If I had money, I will travel.* → ✔ *I would travel*.",
      "- Nunca *would* después de *if* (salvo para ofrecer algo educado: *If you would sit down…*).",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *would* /wʊd/ · *wouldn't* /ˈwʊdnt/ · *mansion* /ˈmænʃn/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "If I would win...",
        "right": "If I won...",
        "note": "If + pasado."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "If I was rich, I will travel.",
        "right": "If I were rich, I would travel.",
        "note": "Would, no will."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
